# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-11, RC-7). L §5.14: "Where q's parts are fewer than the amount, the take goes on down the
# order, which is tracing's own rule". w1 is paid from tomek's (50.00) and takes 70.00: tomek's 50.00, then 20.00 of
# ania's (the next in the order): ania 80.00, tomek 0.00, w1's leg 50.00 of tomek's and 20.00 of ania's.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in withdrawals and k.owner == w.paid_from then 0 else 1
kind withdrawals: transfers
  attr paid_from: key persons
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
input w1_day: date
input w1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t1_amt
move w1: withdrawals
  on w1_day
  attr paid_from = tomek
  leg cash from konto to shop amount w1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, w1.cash.amount of tomek, w1.cash.amount of ania

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 50.00 PLN
  w1_day = 2026-03-01
  w1_amt = 70.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (80.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
